{"diagnosis": "Loopback divider 64 send 0xa5 was received as 0x00 causing TRAP: uart data mismatch got 0x00 want 0xa5 and tohost FAIL 0xdead (picosoc/picosoc.v:190, picosoc/simpleuart.v:20). Receiver default state picosoc/simpleuart.v:96-102 shifts recv_pattern <= {ser_rx, recv_pattern[7:0]} which is 9-bits and truncates away ser_rx so recv_pattern stays 0. Changing slice to [7:1] restores 8-bit shift-in so state 10 picosoc/simpleuart.v:89-95 latches correct 0xa5.",
"patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -96,7 +96,7 @@
 				default: begin
 					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
- 						recv_pattern <= {ser_rx, recv_pattern[7:0]};
+ 						recv_pattern <= {ser_rx, recv_pattern[7:1]};
 						recv_state <= recv_state + 1;
 						recv_divcnt <= 0;
 					end
",
"expected": "tohost PASS, no TRAP, uart loopback got 0xa5 want 0xa5"}

